[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3555202707","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112975#issuecomment-3555202707","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112975","id":3555202707,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7T6BaT","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T00:28:42Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T00:28:42Z","body":"I think you could add some example usages in one file, like I did in #96622.\r\nbtw I still think we should make an exception and allow `auto` for factory methods >_>","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3555202707/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3555218500","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112975#issuecomment-3555218500","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112975","id":3555218500,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7T6FRE","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T00:35:15Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T00:36:53Z","body":"> I think you could add some example usages in one file, like I did in #96622. \r\n\r\nWell, example uses are simple enough:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nVector<int> vector = Vector<int>::make(1, 2, 3); // [1, 2, 3]\r\nVector<Variant> vector = Vector<Variant>::make(1, 2, 3); // [1, 2, 3]\r\nArray array = Array::make(Array::make(1), 2, 3); // [[1], 2, 3]\r\n// etc.\r\n```\r\n\r\n> btw I still think we should make an exception and allow `auto` for factory methods >_>\r\n\r\nI've found so far it isn't actually that bad, in many cases the type is short like `Array`.\r\nBut yea, I wouldn't be against it either.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3555218500/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3559407497","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112975#issuecomment-3559407497","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112975","id":3559407497,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UKD-J","user":{"login":"aaronp64","id":136198872,"node_id":"U_kgDOCB462A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/136198872?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronp64","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T18:14:55Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T18:14:55Z","body":"It looks like there's two steps involved - `memnew_placement` the items into `RelocateInitData`'s array, then `memcpy` into the container.  Is it possible to skip `RelocateInitData`, and just `memnew_placement` into the container directly?  Something like below (haven't compiled/tested, might need some changes):\r\n\r\n```c++\r\ntemplate <typename... Args>\r\nstatic LocalVector make(Args &&...args) {\r\n\tstatic_assert(sizeof...(Args) > 0);\r\n\tLocalVector result;\r\n\tCRASH_COND(result.reserve(sizeof...(Args)));\r\n\tsize_t i = -1;\r\n\t(memnew_placement(result.data + (++i), T(std::forward<Args>(args))), ...);\r\n\tresult.count = sizeof...(Args);\r\n\treturn result;\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3559407497/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3559488458","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112975#issuecomment-3559488458","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112975","id":3559488458,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UKXvK","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-20T18:34:43Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T19:48:41Z","body":"> It looks like there's two steps involved - `memnew_placement` the items into `RelocateInitData`'s array, then `memcpy` into the container. Is it possible to skip `RelocateInitData`, and just `memnew_placement` into the container directly? Something like below (haven't compiled/tested, might need some changes):\r\n> \r\n> ```c++\r\n> template <typename... Args>\r\n> static LocalVector make(Args &&...args) {\r\n> \tstatic_assert(sizeof...(Args) > 0);\r\n> \tLocalVector result;\r\n> \tCRASH_COND(result.reserve(sizeof...(Args)));\r\n> \tsize_t i = -1;\r\n> \t(memnew_placement(result.data + (++i), T(std::forward<Args>(args))), ...);\r\n> \tresult.count = sizeof...(Args);\r\n> \treturn result;\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nYes, this would be an option as well.\r\nHowever, I decided against it for three reasons:\r\n\r\n- By resolving the `Args...` as close as possible to the caller, we can increase the likelihood of the calls being inlined and optimized. In the case of `LocalVector`, this makes little difference, but in the case of `Vector`, it may.\r\n- The `RelocateInitList` syntax might be needed in some locations anyway, for encapsulation purposes. For example, `Array` currently does not expose its internal structure, which we may want to preserve.\r\n- The `RelocateInitList` syntax could be exposed to GDExtension. The `template` version cannot.\r\n\r\n`memcpy` is extremely cheap, so I don't expect it to have a noticeable performance impact for the cases in which `::make` might be called.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3559488458/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3664231224","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112975#issuecomment-3664231224","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112975","id":3664231224,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aZ7s4","user":{"login":"MrModez","id":10527354,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTI3MzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10527354?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrModez","html_url":"https://github.com/MrModez","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrModez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrModez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrModez/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrModez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrModez/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrModez/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrModez/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrModez/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MrModez/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-17T08:32:38Z","updated_at":"2025-12-17T08:34:16Z","body":"shouldn't those static make functions also be marked as `_FORCE_INLINE_` ?\r\n\r\nalso how about marking deprecated constructors with the `[[deprecated]]` attribute?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3664231224/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3664288100","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112975#issuecomment-3664288100","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112975","id":3664288100,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aaJlk","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-17T08:48:48Z","updated_at":"2025-12-17T08:49:54Z","body":"> shouldn't those static make functions also be marked as `_FORCE_INLINE_` ?\n\nMaybe. In optimized builds i don't think it will make a difference.\n\n> also how about marking deprecated constructors with the `[[deprecated]]` attribute?\n\nDeprecating or removing the old constructors will be up for a follow up.\nUnfortunately we can't mark them as deprecated until we remove internal use of them because otherwise we'll start compiling with hundreds of warnings until it's all fixed. That could be a distraction for other developers.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3664288100/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]